  "description": "The Te Tai Tokerau Party is an electorate-focused indigenous rights party. It was founded in 2026 to support the candidacy of former Te Pati Māori and current MP Mariameno Kapa-Kingi. Kapa-Kingi was suspended by her party following accusations of mismanaging funds. She successfully challenged that suspension in the High Court. With a background in Iwi-run social services, Kapa-Kingi was most prominently the Te Pati Māori spokesperson for housing, children, and Oranga Tamariki.  ",
